WEBVTT

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.330
I'm activating it.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.500
Activate

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.250
We'll teach them a lesson!

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.900
I feel like I'm going crazy

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:56.360
I like nice songs

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:00.830
and I want you to listen to them too

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:05.830
Whenever

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:11.460
I sing a song

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:15.050
I hear a voice coming from the microphone

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:17.510
wishing me the best

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.220
I want you

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.760
to hear it too

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:22.640
Good luck!

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:26.600
You can't show your love

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:32.320
just with niceties

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:37.200
That won't provide comfort

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:41.450
Whenever I say something

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:47.500
out of the ordinary

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:50.960
in my heart

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:53.460
I wish you the best

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.010
I want you

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.630
to hear that line

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:58.630
Good luck!

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:19.450
Dream

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:23.200
We're here.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.920
W-Wait!

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:35.000
Suzumoto Auto, LLC
Repairs & Character Decals

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.170
Hey, what do you think you're doing?

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:45.430
Oh, this is...

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:49.130
Wait... is that you, Yukina?

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:51.620
Noriko...

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:56.460
What does "communal property" mean?

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.040
Unattended vehicles are confiscated immediately.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.680
We repaint them to match the scenery here,

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.120
and then rent them out to tourists.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.260
You can't do that!

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:08.860
They were only left there because people thought we were thieves and arrested us!

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:11.800
Mom, I told you what happened, didn't I?

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:13.200
Give them their motorcycles back.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.660
They need to—

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.930
They need to repaint them if they want to run.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:17.590
Huh?

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:21.280
Then they won't stand out in town as much.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:22.590
So...

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.910
She does seem to have a point...

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:26.840
She also seems to just want to paint them.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:27.970
Another bowl!

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:33.400
Um, why do you believe us, Noriko?

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:35.900
Well,

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:40.070
there isn't anyone who could steal that stone from the captain.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:41.490
It's plain impossible.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:47.240
Anyway, if you knew this kid,
you shoulda helped us sooner.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:50.660
I didn't even recognize her.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:54.280
Last time we met, her hair was longer,

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.950
and she wore glasses and cute clothes.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:59.760
Thanks for your help that time.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.440
You seem a little gloomier now.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.880
R-Really?

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:07.760
Hey, what's that?

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:13.980
Oh, I drew that to thank them for their help.

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:16.460
You can draw, Yukina?

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:17.710
What's it a drawing of?

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.260
They're portraits.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.240
Of who?

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:22.980
Of them.

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:27.930
Is that your dad?

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:31.870
Oh, him? He was a novelist who was freeloading at our place.

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:38.150
He may look a little dorky, but he was a vigilante squad leader
in the past, and the first pilot of the Tokyo Tower Robot.

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:39.380
Wow...

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:43.240
You look like one big happy family.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.180
Yeah.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.310
He's gone?

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:48.690
Yep, he went on a journey.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:54.200
As the founder of Always Comima, he was treated like a god,

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:58.060
but his novels didn't sell at all.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:58.810
Oh!

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:01.310
What's the matter, Mom?

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:04.040
Don't tell me he's...

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:04.780
He's what?

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:06.480
The perpetrator!

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.530
The one who stole the captain's stone.

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:10.750
What? Mr. Akutabi?

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:15.650
The warnings and crime declarations were all written on gridded paper, right?

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:19.330
Remember how he always wrote his manuscripts by hand?

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:22.600
Th-That's true...

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:26.800
Maybe he joined up with the people that hate Comima to get back at the people that ignored his books!

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.750
Well, I don't think he was the kind of person to—

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:31.620
No, I'm sure that's it, Mom!

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:34.260
That means this mess is our problem.

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:35.930
It has nothing to do with you.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:38.310
Get away before they catch you.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:39.200
But...

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:43.860
If you're caught, you'll be tortured until they get you to confess.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:46.130
Wh-What if we don't confess?

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.570
You'll be tortured until you do.

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:52.950
In this country, theft is as serious a crime as murder,

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:52.990
Suspicion of Plagiarism

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:57.220
because most things that are stolen in Always Comima are as important as—

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:57.250
No, more important than people's lives.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:57.290
Don't allow stealing!!
No, more important than people's lives.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:01.210
No, more important than people's lives.

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:04.090
Then we're really...

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:10.440
The punishment decided by the Knights of the Twin Towers

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:13.440
is to be sent into that huge place where the sovereign lives.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:14.850
That huge place?!

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:19.820
Inside, men are condemned butlers and women are condemned maids,

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:22.110
and they are made to serve day and night without rest.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:25.090
No one has ever returned.

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:29.080
I'm friends with the girl at the southern checkpoint.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:33.480
I'll have her hide your departure until morning, so you should get as far away—

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:34.410
N-No thank you!

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:35.330
Hey!

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:36.490
Nozomi?

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:39.200
I will stay h-here.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:44.950
I-I won't leave until the captain believes us and gives Chi's stone back.

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:46.910
I don't think that's possible.

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:49.130
We should accept her help for now.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:52.430
We can just find Chi a new stone somewhere else.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:56.060
R-Running is no different from admitting we did it.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:58.080
That's why I said we <i>aren't</i> running.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:58.910
I'll get stronger and come—

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:00.240
What'll you do if you don't get stronger?
I'll get stronger and come—

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:00.940
What'll you do if you don't get stronger?

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:03.350
You have to believe that I will!

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:05.570
Then let's believe that she'll believe us!

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:06.650
Stop being so naive!

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:08.610
Masami wouldn't give up!

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.360
Yes, well she's—

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.610
Even when she got stronger, she didn't give up!

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:22.180
I'm sure that's why she could get stronger.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:32.460
Even though... I didn't steal it...

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:38.530
Even though... it's my stone...

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:07.250
So this is what you wanted?

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.930
"I can finally buy him, but I'm still not happy."

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:13.350
That's what your face is saying.

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:14.950
That's not true...

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:18.390
I love him.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:23.620
He was never that popular since the story and his hairstyle were strange,

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:26.770
but he worked hard and never lost heart.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:29.730
He risked his life for those he decided to protect,

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:32.400
and never accepted a reward in return.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.400
Is that right?

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:35.910
What a great guy.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.750
That's not all!

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:41.790
He only lied once, and that was because he didn't want his partner to take the girl he loved...

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:47.580
He... lied...

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:53.130
Sold

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:56.950
I'm sorry, Mr. Momiyama.

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:57.800
I...

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:03.810
The original agreement was for the sale of one stone.

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:05.220
Huh?

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:27.840
It's a little cramped, but you can use this room.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:30.130
There are blankets in the closet.

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:32.460
I stayed here last time, didn't I?

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:35.400
We're sleeping here? Everyone?

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:38.110
That's what she said. Wanna have a pillow fight?

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:39.660
Pillow fight?

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:43.310
You've never had one?
Haven't you ever gone on a school trip?

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:44.970
School trips!

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:48.080
Ai, we're guests here.

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:50.020
I'll help, too.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:51.460
With the pillow fight?

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:52.980
Not that.

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:58.400
To convince the captain to let us look for the stone again, together.

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:02.950
Yeah. Yeah, I'm fine.

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:05.820
Everything's going great. Don't worry.

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:09.200
Yeah, it's not like I'm by myself.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:12.280
Huh? They're all girls... Why?

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:15.880
Dad? I don't need to talk to him...

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:19.090
Forget that—how's Masami?

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:21.640
Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:24.350
What? You told her I left??!

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:25.520
Wha—

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:29.640
Stop!

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:34.440
Hey, Yukippe! Where are you sleeping?

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:38.550
It's fun, right?

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:43.160
Pillow Machine Gun!

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:45.350
Uu, that's not fair!

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:47.830
Hey.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:55.550
Why do you know our childhood nicknames?

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:56.370
Huh?

00:10:56.370 --> 00:11:00.150
Oh, yeah. Did you live nearby when you were little?

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:01.930
I don't think that's it.

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:04.350
I just happened to find out.

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:06.060
How did you find out?

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:08.640
U-Um...

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:13.940
O-O-Oh, n-n-no—

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:26.950
I apologize for bringing them here without permission.

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:28.750
But Captain, these girls are—

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.660
I know, Noriko.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:33.290
I'm sorry.

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:36.670
I'm sorry for suspecting you.

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:38.440
You found it?

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:41.150
Did you find your stone?

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:49.270
I made a mistake.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:51.370
You think "sorry" will cover what you put us through?!

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:53.130
I'm so glad.

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:58.240
So Chi can have her stone back, right?

00:11:58.240 --> 00:11:59.350
Well...

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:09.790
The stone stood for a promise.

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:12.790
A promise to protect Always Comima with the state vigilante squad by my side.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:12.830
Squad Member Application
A promise to protect Always Comima with the state vigilante squad by my side.

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:14.540
A promise to protect Always Comima with the state vigilante squad by my side.

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:23.800
A promise to protect everyone's treasures, and their smiles.

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:34.910
That promise meant everything to me.

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:39.320
I can't believe I let it get pushed aside.

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:45.030
A-Are you all right, Nozomi?

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:47.730
Oh no, did I break it?

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:49.280
The insides came out.

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:50.800
That's it!

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:00.550
Hey, maybe we shouldn't do this after all.

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:02.420
What are you saying?!

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:06.430
I can't help but think about how many people could get hurt.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:09.620
Why can't we get back at them?

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:12.060
We're not doing anything wrong.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:13.600
You're making your parents cry

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:18.690
Besides, this is a drop in the bucket compared to what they've put us through!

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:21.320
Why can't we have

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:23.660
just a little justice?

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:28.020
You thought of that little girl just now, didn't you?

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:29.700
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:33.770
That girl, Akaru, who thought we were fellow cosplayers and helped us.

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:36.370
If it appears in front of that girl...

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:37.770
It would serve her right!

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:39.860
It's all their fault!

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:42.880
Can you forgive the guys who made Tokyo into this?

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:45.510
That looks pretty good on you.

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:47.340
Sh-Shut up!

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:52.800
I won't let it affect me! I won't!

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:55.350
Hey! Look at this!

00:13:58.100 --> 00:13:58.140
What?! Explode?!
<b>As thanks for being
a loyal customer, we
set this evil Takumi
special-order Moving
Surprise to "explode"
when activated,
free of charge.</b>

00:13:58.140 --> 00:13:59.930
What?! Explode?!

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:06.080
Another message?

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:09.750
Moving bomb?! Is it the Dynamite Bombers again?

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:15.750
We only know that they're from Higashi Murayama.

00:14:16.130 --> 00:14:17.910
The bomb was made by the evil Takumi.

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:23.750
Apparently, they ordered a prank toy,
and a bomb was added for free.

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:26.380
A-A bomb?

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:31.910
It looks like a cleaning robot,
but we can't forcibly dismantle it.

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:35.600
I'll find it and take care—

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:36.640
Captain!

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:38.140
Pathetic.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:42.650
Without the Drom Berserker,
I'm just an ordinary cosplaying girl.

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:43.480
Huh?

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:44.650
What do you mean?

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:50.660
That stone pushes people's latent abilities to the limit.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:51.280
Huh?

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:52.260
Really?

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:54.660
Seriously? You can get stronger with that?

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:56.660
No way...

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.750
Chi, is that why you wanted it?

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:05.680
I didn't know.

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:09.060
Didn't you find your stone?

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:11.530
I did, but I don't have it anymore.

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:12.340
Why not?

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:15.910
I sold it to the agent of a certain country.

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:16.560
What?

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:19.000
Momiyama...

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:21.400
Have the cleaning robots return to the charging station.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:22.480
Mom!

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.970
The one that doesn't react to the command is the bomb.

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:28.040
It should have a picture of a trap on it. Hurry!

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:32.460
Comb through every area and find it!

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:35.320
Everyone here, come with me to the charging station!

00:15:44.110 --> 00:15:46.710
This is Momiyama. I'm on my way ba—

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:49.080
Chiaya is... Chiaya is gone!

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:50.340
What?

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:00.350
The bomb was found in Port-02J!

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:03.100
It's heading toward the Twin Towers!

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:11.240
T-minus three minutes until explosion!

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:18.870
T-minus two minutes!

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:24.460
<i>Please let me find it!</i>

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:39.600
T-minus one minute!

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:45.350
Garm!

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:20.640
It's fine.

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:56.130
Take them back to HQ for interrogation.

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:59.550
They were probably also the ones behind the bombing incident six months ago.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:01.930
Tell the truth, Noriko.

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:06.890
Captain.

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:09.850
I am the Dynamite Bomber.

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:12.200
What do you mean?

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:16.150
What blew up that day was an unexploded shell from the Great Tokyo War.

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:16.930
Takumi

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:17.860
As part of the investigative team, I hid that fact
Takumi

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:20.870
As part of the investigative team, I hid that fact

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:23.490
and made up a fictitious anti-Comima organization.

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:24.150
Crime Declaration
and made up a fictitious anti-Comima organization.

00:18:24.150 --> 00:18:25.450
Crime Declaration

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:27.890
Why would you do that?

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:31.750
I didn't want the captain to quit.

00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:36.380
I wanted to keep protecting Comima together forever.

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:39.350
When the captain's stone really did get lost,

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:40.780
I wasn't sure what to do.

00:18:45.570 --> 00:18:46.680
I'm sorry.

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:53.650
I see.

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:57.150
Thanks. You saved me.

00:19:00.040 --> 00:19:01.410
I won't retire!

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:05.370
However, Noriko,

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:08.000
as punishment for your actions, you'll be captain now.

